  "notes": "Behavior-contract inventory derived 2026-08-23 from the ChromeStatus record 5427561449521152 (milestone=152 listing category 'Enabled by default'; API record ship stage Android 152, spec_link null, no flag/OT), the Chrome Help protection-levels article, and the two enterprise policy definitions the record names as the admin controls. The feature has no web API surface and no specification; the inventory is the three public contracts: the warning behavior itself and the two policies. Honest gaps stated in prose: the suspicion signal set is deliberately unpublished (Safe Browsing heuristics), the internal launch bug is corp-only, and no desktop milestone is recorded — the compatibility table carries an explicit 'unknown' row for Chrome desktop rather than inferring one."
